    "text": "To determine the age of the fifth scroll, we need to follow the given condition that each scroll is older than the last by half as many years as the last scroll’s age. Let's denote the age of the first scroll as \\( A_1 \\), the age of the second scroll as \\( A_2 \\), and so on, up to the fifth scroll \\( A_5 \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ A_1 = 4080 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThe age of the second scroll \\( A_2 \\) is:\n\\[ A_2 = A_1 + \\frac{1}{2} A_1 = 4080 + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4080 = 4080 + 2040 = 6120 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThe age of the third scroll \\( A_3 \\) is:\n\\[ A_3 = A_2 + \\frac{1}{2} A_2 = 6120 + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6120 = 6120 + 3060 = 9180 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThe age of the fourth scroll \\( A_4 \\) is:\n\\[ A_4 = A_3 + \\frac{1}{2} A_3 = 9180 + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 9180 = 9180 + 4590 = 13770 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThe age of the fifth scroll \\( A_5 \\) is:\n\\[ A_5 = A_4 + \\frac{1}{2} A_4 = 13770 + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13770 = 13770 + 6885 = 20655 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThus, the age of the fifth scroll is:\n\\[ \\boxed{20655} \\]",
